      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood’s first homes were built after the 1906 earthquake, when many contractors focused on larger projects and the subdivision slowed.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://nagleepark.org/naglee-park-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "By 1910, every one of the roughly 600 lots had sold, and the Naglee Park Investment Company dissolved that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://nagleepark.org/naglee-park-history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Naglee Park’s historic homes are so distinctive that a local inventory project is cataloguing them for San Jose’s official historic list.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
